  {
   "id": "ZYgjJICZAwAJ",
   "from": "Terrence Jorgensen",
   "author": "3fe90052fbf2f899",
   "date": "2020-03-21T14:07:44Z",
   "subject": "Re: lavInspect questions: Thresholds and Sigma Matrix",
   "parts": [
    [
     2,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\"><blockquote class=\"gmail_quote\" style=\"margin:0;margin-left:0.8ex;border-left:1px #ccc solid;padding-left:1ex\"><div dir=\"ltr\"><div style=\"font-size:small\">Can someone explain why the statements below do not return the same values? <span style=\"font-size:13px\"> </span></div></div></blockquote></div>"
    ],
    [
     1,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\"><blockquote class=\"gmail_quote\" style=\"margin:0;margin-left:0.8ex;border-left:1px #ccc solid;padding-left:1ex\"><div dir=\"ltr\"><div style=\"font-size:small\"><br></div><div style=\"font-size:small\">lavInspect(mod,what = &quot;est&quot;)$tau<br></div></div></blockquote><div><br></div><div>These are the estimated thresholds, interpreted relative to whatever the model-implied means/variances of latent item responses are.</div><div><br></div><blockquote class=\"gmail_quote\" style=\"margin:0;margin-left:0.8ex;border-left:1px #ccc solid;padding-left:1ex\"><div dir=\"ltr\"><div style=\"font-size:small\">lavInspect(mod.fit,what = &quot;th&quot;)<br></div></div></blockquote><div> </div><div>These are the model-implied *standardized* thresholds (i.e., interpreted relative to latent item responses that are assumed standard normal), which are merely implied by the estimated model parameters (including thresholds and variances).</div><div><br></div><div>When using parameterization = &quot;delta&quot; in models without equality constraints, these will typically be the same because the estimated thresholds are already interpreted relative to standard normal latent item responses.</div></div>"
    ],
    [
     2,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\"><div><br></div><div> </div><blockquote class=\"gmail_quote\" style=\"margin:0;margin-left:0.8ex;border-left:1px #ccc solid;padding-left:1ex\"><div dir=\"ltr\"><div style=\"font-size:small\">lavInspect(mod,what = &quot;sigma&quot;)<br>lavInspect(mod.fit,what = &quot;vy&quot;)</div></div></blockquote><div><br></div></div>"
    ],
    [
     1,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\"><div>The latter merely returns model-implied variances, which appear on the diagonal of the Sigma matrix returned by the former.</div><div><br></div><div><div><div>Terrence D. Jorgensen</div><div>Assistant Professor, Methods and Statistics</div><div>Research Institute for Child Development and Education, the University of Amsterdam</div><div><a href=\"http://www.uva.nl/profile/t.d.jorgensen\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=http://www.uva.nl/profile/t.d.jorgensen&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792422250635000&amp;usg=AOvVaw03LwWLntCRLfKGEKw2wdya\">http://www.uva.nl/profile/t.d.jorgensen</a></div></div><div><br></div><div></div></div></div>"
    ]
