  {
   "id": "kOa6BVy1BQAJ",
   "from": "Hugo Harada",
   "author": "73fb61795976b321",
   "date": "2020-03-22T04:47:04Z",
   "subject": "Re: lavInspect questions: Thresholds and Sigma Matrix",
   "parts": [
    [
     1,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\"><div class=\"gmail_default\" style=\"font-size:small\">Hi Terrence,</div><div class=\"gmail_default\" style=\"font-size:small\"><br></div><div class=\"gmail_default\" style=\"font-size:small\">Thank you for your reply.</div></div>"
    ],
    [
     2,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\"><div class=\"gmail_default\" style=\"font-size:small\"><br></div><div class=\"gmail_default\" style=\"font-size:small\"><span><i><font color=\"#ff00ff\"><blockquote class=\"gmail_quote\" style=\"margin:0px 0px 0px 0.8ex;border-left:1px solid rgb(204,204,204);padding-left:1ex\"><div dir=\"ltr\"><div>lavInspect(mod,what = &quot;sigma&quot;)<br>lavInspect(mod.fit,what = &quot;vy&quot;)</div></div></blockquote><div><br></div></font></i></span><div><i><font color=\"#ff00ff\">The latter merely returns model-implied variances, which appear on the diagonal of the Sigma matrix returned by the former.</font></i></div><div><br></div></div></div>"
    ],
    [
     1,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\"><div class=\"gmail_default\" style=\"font-size:small\">That is exactly what I was expecting but I am getting results different from that. See below. </div><div class=\"gmail_default\" style=\"font-size:small\"><br></div><div class=\"gmail_default\" style=\"font-size:small\"><div><img src=\"https://groups.google.com/group/lavaan/attach/5b55c05bae690/image.png?part=0.1&amp;view=1\" alt=\"image.png\" width=\"385\" height=\"168\"><br></div><div>The is as below. </div><div><br></div><div>rm(list=ls())<br>if(!require(lavaan)) install.packages(&quot;lavaan&quot;); library(lavaan)<br>if(!require(rockchalk)) install.packages(&quot;rockchalk&quot;); library(rockchalk)<br><br><br>N &lt;- 2000 ## subjects<br>I= 4  # Number of Items<br>PL=2 # Logistic Model (1,2,3 parameters)<br>rho&lt;-0.7<br><br><br>if (PL==1) {a = rep(1,I)} else {a = runif(I,0.5, 2.5)}    # U(0.5 , 2.5)<br>b = runif(I,-2, 2.0)     # U(-2 , 2)<br>d=-a*b # MIRT trabalha com o intercepto (d=-ab) e nao com a dificuldade (b)<br><br>Sigma &lt;- lazyCor(c(rho,rho*rho,rho)) #Matriz de Covariancia AR(1)<br>Theta &lt;- mvrnorm(n=N, mu=c(0,0.5,1), Sigma )<br><br>dat =simdata(a=a,d=d,N=N,itemtype = &#39;2PL&#39;, Theta = matrix(Theta[,1],ncol=1,nrow = length(Theta[,1])))<br><br>colnames(dat) &lt;- c(&quot;y2w1&quot;,&quot;y2w2&quot;,&quot;y2w3&quot;,&quot;y2w4&quot;)<br><br>#expected thresholds<br>prop &lt;- colSums(dat)/nrow(dat)<br>prop<br>th &lt;- qnorm(1-prop)<br>th<br><br><br># Specify Model Parameters for numerical itens<br># 3 indicators with latent variables. <br><br>mod2ind3lv1.simple&lt;- function(){}<br><br>mod2ind3lv1.simple &lt;- &#39;<br><br>lv1 =~ l1*y2w1 + l2*y2w2 + l3*y2w3 <br>l1 + l2 + l3 == 3 <br>lv1 ~ 1<br><br># ## thresholds link LIRs to observed items<br>y2w1 | thr1*t1<br>y2w2 | thr2*t1<br>y2w3 | thr3*t1<br>thr1 + thr2 +thr3 ==0<br><br>&#39;<br><br>sem.model &lt;- mod2ind3lv1.simple<br><br><br>rm(mod2ind3lv1.fit)<br>mod2ind3lv1.fit &lt;- lavaan(model = sem.model, <br>                          data = dat, <br>                          <a href=\"http://std.lv\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=http://std.lv&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792422250639000&amp;usg=AOvVaw3bkq-0hVQ2_pW3aJCMyDp8\">std.lv</a> = FALSE,<br>                          int.ov.free = TRUE,<br>                          int.lv.free = TRUE,<br>                          meanstructure =TRUE,<br>                          auto.fix.first = FALSE,<br>                          auto.var = TRUE,<br>                          <a href=\"http://auto.th\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=http://auto.th&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792422250639000&amp;usg=AOvVaw1TINzeLUAoW9EZIP8oTTIE\">auto.th</a> = TRUE,<br>                          ordered = c(&quot;y2w1&quot;,&quot;y2w2&quot;,&quot;y2w3&quot;),<br>                          parameterization = &quot;theta&quot;)<br><br><br>summary(mod2ind3lv1.fit)<br><br>lavInspect(mod2ind3lv1.fit,what = &quot;est&quot;)$tau<br>lavInspect(mod2ind3lv1.fit,what = &quot;th&quot;)<br><br>lavInspect(mod2ind3lv1.fit,what = &quot;sigma&quot;)<br>lavInspect(mod2ind3lv1.fit,what = &quot;vy&quot;)<br><br><br>Looking forward to hearing from you.</div><div><br></div><div>Hugo<br><br></div><div><br></div><div><br></div><div><br></div></div></div><br><div class=\"gmail_quote\"></div>"
    ],
